occupationalSummary:
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;This occupation is found in organisations of all sizes, including small, medium-sized, large, and global organisations, across the public, private, and third sectors. Individuals in this role generally work within an organisation’s accounts or finance department, or within a professional accountancy firm.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;The broad purpose of the occupation is to manage and implement accounting and finance systems and processes that support decision-making in line with organisational strategy. This is achieved through the application of technical and technological knowledge and skills across all aspects of accounting and finance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;Responsibilities may include managing the operations of the accounting or finance function; supporting senior management and other departments by providing timely financial information and reports; ensuring compliance with internal controls, HMRC requirements, legislation, regulations, and ethical and professional standards; monitoring the efficient, effective, and economical operation of systems using appropriate technology; and identifying issues, recommending solutions, and providing advice to internal and or external clients.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;In their daily work, an employee in this occupation interacts with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders, including directors and senior managers, clients and customers, suppliers, lenders, government agencies, auditors, and other professionals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;A typical day may involve working in an office environment and overseeing activities such as data entry, control account reconciliations, budgeting and forecasting, trend analysis, and monthly, quarterly, and annual reporting. The role may also include researching and recommending solutions to support decision-makers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;An accounting finance manager works both independently and as part of, or while leading, a team. They play a pivotal role in bridging the gap between the strategic and operational levels of an organisation by applying a broad range of technical, technological, and interpersonal skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;An employee in this occupation will be responsible for contributing to and implementing business plans and strategy, as determined by senior management, and for managing the systems and operations that support their delivery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;This includes overseeing operational activities; monitoring, analysing, and controlling systems and procedures; and ensuring the efficient, economical, and effective use of resources. The role also involves managing the budgeting process, analysing variances, investigating and explaining changes, and making recommendations to support decision-making.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;In addition, an individual in this role will monitor and control cash flow, identify trends, and forecast future requirements. They will also be involved in recruiting and training staff in line with organisational strategy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 115%&quot;&gt;The role requires conducting regular and detailed analysis of financial and operational data and providing accurate financial and management information to meet the needs of internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
